# AUDIT-AI: Automated Public Procurement Anomaly & Forensic Engine

## Project Overview
**AUDIT-AI** is an end-to-end machine learning and document forensic platform designed to screen public procurement tender submissions. It ingests raw `.pdf` tender application documents, extracts multi-modal financial, corporate, and textual features, and feeds them into a trained **PyTorch Deep Autoencoder** to detect structural anomalies, bid-rigging risks, and synthetic fraud in real time.

---

## Project Directory Structure

```text
project/
├── model/
│   ├── nnm.py                  # PyTorch model architecture & normal-baseline training pipeline
│   ├── autoencoder_model.pth   # Generated trained model checkpoint & normalization state
│   ├── procurement_training_dataset.csv # Master tabular training dataset (~4,653 rows, 66 features)
│   └── [Relational CSVs: bids.csv, contracts.csv, documents.csv, payments.csv, tenders.csv, vendors.csv]
├── backend/
│   ├── main.py                 # FastAPI application endpoint & PDF regex text parser
│   └── requirements.txt        # Python backend dependencies
└── frontend/
    └── index.html              # Responsive single-page web UI for PDF uploads & risk analytics
